Until I'm not completely mistaken, the source tells us 
that unless you have negative luck you get either 
your wished-for plus or +0.  I did some calculations 
and came up with the following success probabilities 
for wishing for +x:  

If 0 < x <= 5, we have 

x       Prob("Get +x")

1       80.612%

2       60.408%

3       40.204%

4       20.090%

5       0.038%

For x > max{5, XL/3}, we have Prob("Get +x") = 0, while 
for 5 < x <= max{5, XL/3}, we have Prob("Get +x") = (1/3)^x.  
(Thus, in theory one could get +10 weapons when at Lvl 30, but 
in average only every 3^10 = 59 049 trials.) 

However, I am a bit suspicious about these results, since 
it seems that the test (spe > otmp->spe) plays almost no 
role and could just as well be left out.  

